FILESYSTEM - Computah OS library
(generated from docs/API.md)

The virtual file tree. Every filesystem component
is mounted somewhere under /: the boot drive at /,
the temporary filesystem at /tmp, other drives at
/mnt/<first 3 address characters>.

filesystem.canonical(path) -> string

The absolute form of a path, with . and ..
resolved (.. never goes above /). Relative paths
are taken from the working directory. Doesn't
follow links (see realPath).

filesystem.concat(path, ...) -> string

Joins path parts with / and resolves ./...
Absolute if the first part is.

  filesystem.concat("/home", "user", "../x.lua")  --> "/home/x.lua"

filesystem.segments(path) -> table

The parts of a path: segments("/a/b/../c") → {"a",
"c"}.

filesystem.path(path) -> string

The directory part of a path, ending in /:
path("/a/b/c") → "/a/b/".

filesystem.name(path) -> string

The last part of a path: name("/a/b/c.lua") →
"c.lua".

filesystem.mount(fs, path) -> boolean

Mounts a filesystem at a path.

- fs: a filesystem proxy or a component address.
- Returns nil, reason if it isn't a filesystem or
  something is already mounted there.

filesystem.umount(target) -> boolean

Unmounts by mount path, by proxy, or by component
address (or unique prefix). Returns whether
anything was unmounted.

filesystem.mounts() -> iterator

Iterates over mounts: for proxy, path in
filesystem.mounts() do ... end.

filesystem.get(path) -> proxy, relative, mountPath

The filesystem proxy holding a path, the path
relative to that filesystem, and where it is
mounted. Follows links. Returns nil, reason if
nothing is mounted there.

filesystem.proxy(filter) -> proxy

The proxy of a filesystem by address prefix or by
label (mounted or not). Returns nil, reason if
none matches.

  local disk = filesystem.proxy("Computah OS")

filesystem.exists(path) -> boolean

Whether a file, directory, mount point or link
exists at the path.

filesystem.isDirectory(path) -> boolean

Whether the path is a directory (or a mount point,
or a link to a directory).

filesystem.size(path) -> number

Size of a file in bytes (0 for directories and
missing files).

filesystem.lastModified(path) -> number

When a file was last changed, in milliseconds
since the epoch (0 if unknown).

filesystem.isReadOnly(path) -> boolean

Whether the filesystem holding the path is read-
only.

filesystem.list(path) -> iterator

Iterates over a directory's entries, sorted;
directories end with /. Includes mount points and
links in that directory. Returns nil, "no such
directory" if it isn't one.

  for name in filesystem.list("/home") do print(name) end

filesystem.makeDirectory(path) -> boolean

Creates a directory and any missing parent
directories. Returns false if it exists, nil,
reason on failure (read-only, no space).

filesystem.remove(path) -> boolean

Removes a file, or a directory with everything in
it. For a link, removes the link (not its target).

filesystem.rename(from, to) -> boolean

Moves or renames. Across filesystems, files are
copied then removed (directories can't be moved
across filesystems).

filesystem.copy(from, to) -> boolean

Copies a file. Returns nil, reason on failure.

filesystem.link(target, linkpath) -> boolean

Creates a symbolic link: linkpath then refers to
target (a file or directory, relative targets are
taken from the link's directory). Links are
virtual, like in OpenOS: they live in memory and
disappear at reboot (they do survive the computer
being saved and loaded). Returns nil, "file
already exists" if linkpath exists.

  filesystem.link("/mnt/a1b", "/data")

filesystem.isLink(path) -> boolean, target

Whether the path is a link, and where it points.

filesystem.realPath(path) -> string

The canonical path with every link followed.

filesystem.open(path[, mode]) -> handle

Opens a file without buffering; normally use
io.open. mode is "r" (default), "w", "a",
optionally with "b". Returns a handle with
:read(n), :write(data), :seek(whence, offset) and
:close(), or nil, reason.

filesystem.readAll(path) -> string

The whole contents of a file, or nil, reason.

filesystem.writeAll(path, data) -> boolean

Replaces a file's contents. Returns nil, reason on
failure.

filesystem.mountAll()

Mounts every filesystem that isn't mounted yet at
/mnt/<prefix>, and keeps doing so as drives are
added and removed. The OS calls this at boot.

filesystem.isAutorunEnabled() -> boolean

Whether /autorun.lua on a newly added drive (for
example a floppy put in a disk drive) runs
automatically. Off by default; stored in
/etc/filesystem.cfg.

filesystem.setAutorunEnabled(enabled)

Turns autorun on or off. The autorun file runs as
a background process with its path as the
argument.
